WEBVTT

00:14.229 --> 00:16.106
What kind of excuse
are you trying to make?

00:16.189 --> 00:17.357
What?

00:17.941 --> 00:20.360
You could've made up for it
in high school.

00:20.986 --> 00:23.864
It's natural to have people
better than you.

00:23.947 --> 00:25.365
But that's not it.

00:25.949 --> 00:27.242
That's not the point.

00:29.619 --> 00:30.912
<i>What!</i>

00:30.996 --> 00:32.247
Of course...

00:33.248 --> 00:36.752
It's easy to say the right thing
when you're not the one going through it.

00:49.431 --> 00:50.724
I mean, am I wrong?

00:50.807 --> 00:52.809
You're so freaking annoying.

00:52.893 --> 00:56.605
That self-righteous look on your face
is really ticking me off.

00:57.606 --> 01:00.567
Stay out of this. It's not like
I'm going to see Natsu anymore anyway.

01:01.151 --> 01:04.905
You're the one who came at her first
for no reason!

01:05.489 --> 01:08.909
That's because she was out playing around
after saying she'd win nationals!

01:08.992 --> 01:11.078
She's been going to practice diligently!

01:11.161 --> 01:12.662
She used to practice way more.

01:12.746 --> 01:14.790
She practically lived
and breathed basketball.

01:14.873 --> 01:18.502
She only got that good
because she worked harder than anyone!

01:18.585 --> 01:20.921
She can't get to the top
while having a social life.

01:25.926 --> 01:27.928
<i>Wait.</i>

01:28.595 --> 01:32.182
<i>She's just worried about Chinatsu Senpai.</i>

01:32.265 --> 01:33.934
Ms. Goto?

01:34.017 --> 01:36.937
Mr. Inomata? Is something wrong?

01:37.813 --> 01:39.189
It's nothing.

01:41.066 --> 01:45.320
<i>I knew it,
things can't stay this way between them.</i>

01:49.491 --> 01:53.662
BLUE BOX SEASON 2

03:16.786 --> 03:20.540
EPISODE 28
THEY'RE ONE AND THE SAME

03:32.093 --> 03:33.637
Good morning.

03:36.556 --> 03:39.935
Taiki, pack that food
into the bento boxes!

03:40.602 --> 03:42.229
Did you oversleep?

03:42.312 --> 03:44.356
It's not my fault
Korean dramas are so good!

03:45.106 --> 03:47.234
<i>What a childish reason.</i>

03:48.026 --> 03:49.361
What about Chinatsu Senpai?

03:49.945 --> 03:51.821
I sent her on ahead.

03:51.905 --> 03:54.366
She has the Winter Cup
coming up after all.

03:55.700 --> 03:58.245
Bring a bento box to her, would you?

03:58.328 --> 03:59.996
Leave it in front of her clubroom.

04:00.080 --> 04:01.122
Okay, fine.

04:03.083 --> 04:05.710
<i>Chinatsu Senpai's packed lunch.</i>

04:06.211 --> 04:07.045
GOOD LUCK

04:07.128 --> 04:10.632
<i>Would she be happy
if I did something like this?</i>

04:12.050 --> 04:13.635
<i>Not that I would.</i>

04:14.261 --> 04:16.388
<i>I'll give her the bigger sausage.</i>

04:16.471 --> 04:18.640
<i>And plenty of vegetables.</i>

04:18.723 --> 04:20.809
<i>And the best-looking tamagoyaki.</i>

04:23.687 --> 04:25.981
There's no way you're going to get
the lid to fit.

04:26.064 --> 04:27.399
I was afraid of that.

04:29.067 --> 04:30.360
I'm off!

04:37.659 --> 04:38.660
Taiki!

04:39.995 --> 04:41.705
You're late today.

04:41.788 --> 04:43.498
I stopped by the convenience store.

04:43.581 --> 04:45.166
- Next!
- Okay!

04:47.002 --> 04:48.295
- Next!
- Okay!

04:50.380 --> 04:52.799
The basketball team
has a tournament coming up, right?

04:53.717 --> 04:58.305
The whole vibe in the gym changes
when a club has an upcoming tournament.

04:58.388 --> 05:00.557
It's quiet and tense.

05:01.433 --> 05:03.560
It's like we can feel their tension too.

05:04.227 --> 05:05.061
Yeah.

05:09.065 --> 05:10.150
I know what you mean.

05:11.234 --> 05:12.277
Good morning.

05:12.360 --> 05:13.403
Morning.

05:15.822 --> 05:17.073
Morning.

05:21.328 --> 05:23.079
- Morning.
- Bye.

05:26.666 --> 05:28.001
Don't worry.

05:29.169 --> 05:32.839
Despite her attitude, she's killing it
with her rhythmic gymnastics.

05:33.465 --> 05:38.178
Looks like you had less of an effect
on Hina's life than I thought.

05:41.181 --> 05:43.391
<i>What is she implying?</i>

06:00.700 --> 06:03.912
Whose lunch is this?

06:03.995 --> 06:05.747
That's mine.

06:21.054 --> 06:23.139
We need to hurry, Chinatsu.

06:23.223 --> 06:24.224
Okay.

06:26.976 --> 06:27.894
I'm open!

06:28.603 --> 06:29.896
Push it!

06:29.979 --> 06:31.898
Let's get one back!

06:37.237 --> 06:38.655
Get back on D!

06:43.159 --> 06:44.452
Ten-minute break, everyone!

06:44.536 --> 06:45.745
Okay!

06:55.088 --> 06:57.382
Yuna, do you have a second?

06:58.133 --> 06:59.384
What is it?

07:00.051 --> 07:03.888
That last play, you could've gone
for the shot yourself.

07:04.514 --> 07:07.392
They had Saya completely covered.

07:07.976 --> 07:12.564
No pressure, but I think it's okay
if you play more aggressively.

07:12.647 --> 07:16.192
I'd be happy to run drills with you
after practice or in the morning.

07:16.276 --> 07:17.402
Sorry!

07:17.485 --> 07:19.154
I already know!

07:19.779 --> 07:23.908
I know I'm no good,
and that I'm dragging everyone down.

07:24.701 --> 07:25.910
But you know what?

07:26.536 --> 07:30.790
Don't think that everyone
can work as hard as you.

07:33.501 --> 07:36.421
Sorry! I lost it for a second there!

07:36.504 --> 07:38.423
It's okay.

07:38.506 --> 07:42.427
I'm not perfect either.
Let's just do our best together.

08:09.287 --> 08:11.206
You're here first again?

08:11.289 --> 08:12.582
What?

08:12.665 --> 08:15.084
Don't you ever want to skip practice
and play games instead?

08:15.960 --> 08:19.088
But I started basketball
later than everyone else.

08:20.006 --> 08:24.135
So I have to practice
at least an hour extra a day to catch up.

08:24.219 --> 08:28.556
An hour a day would mean
an extra day every 24 days,

08:28.640 --> 08:33.520
so one year's worth would be...

08:33.603 --> 08:35.355
I don't have time to do anything else!

08:36.606 --> 08:39.359
It's one thing to think that,
and another to actually do it.

08:39.984 --> 08:43.363
Being able to do that is your talent.

09:10.473 --> 09:12.267
5:30 ALARM
STOP - SNOOZE

09:21.109 --> 09:25.405
Don't think that everyone
can work as hard as you.

09:26.698 --> 09:27.865
Crap!

09:56.227 --> 09:57.437
Good morning.

09:57.520 --> 09:59.188
Good morning!

09:59.272 --> 10:00.440
Good morning.

10:01.024 --> 10:03.151
I left your lunch on the table.

10:03.234 --> 10:05.194
It's nicely packed today.

10:05.862 --> 10:07.196
Since someone didn't oversleep.

10:07.280 --> 10:08.656
Excuse me?

10:08.740 --> 10:11.492
You should be grateful
that I wake up early every morning

10:11.576 --> 10:13.244
to match your schedules.

10:13.828 --> 10:15.622
I am grateful.

10:15.705 --> 10:16.998
Thank you.

10:17.081 --> 10:20.752
In that case, you can pick up
a cake for me from the shop.

10:21.336 --> 10:23.004
Don't get carried away.

10:30.178 --> 10:32.263
- Hey, Taiki.
- Yeah?

10:32.347 --> 10:36.768
Have you ever felt like
skipping morning practice?

10:38.144 --> 10:43.274
<i>I have a feeling I would've
if it weren't for Chinatsu Senpai.</i>

10:45.735 --> 10:47.779
Of course I have.

10:47.862 --> 10:50.531
Like some days,
I don't want to get out of bed.

10:52.158 --> 10:56.371
But when that happens,
I just imagine my future self.

10:56.954 --> 11:00.041
And chances are,
I'm regretting falling back to sleep

11:00.958 --> 11:04.045
and hating myself a little for it.

11:04.671 --> 11:07.298
So when I imagine all that,
it motivates me to wake up.

11:18.935 --> 11:21.104
You're so hardworking.

11:22.397 --> 11:24.065
<i>You're one to talk!</i>

11:44.961 --> 11:47.213
<i>If she's asking me that,</i>

11:47.713 --> 11:51.217
<i>does that mean she feels like
skipping practice too sometimes?</i>

11:52.510 --> 11:54.220
<i>I bet she does.</i>

11:54.804 --> 11:57.974
<i>I mean, she originally started all of this
because of Yumeka.</i>

11:58.599 --> 12:02.979
<i>But to keep going without taking a break
is so like Chinatsu Senpai.</i>

12:07.692 --> 12:10.027
<i>Yumeka has the wrong idea.</i>

12:11.070 --> 12:14.532
<i>Yes, Chinatsu Senpai continues
to work hard on her own.</i>

12:15.700 --> 12:18.619
<i>But that's only because she has a goal.</i>

12:19.454 --> 12:21.622
<i>It's not that it isn't hard.</i>

12:22.623 --> 12:27.712
<i>I wish Yumeka
had stuck by Chinatsu Senpai's side.</i>

12:30.590 --> 12:32.133
Where's the girls' basketball team?

12:32.216 --> 12:34.510
They had a practice game this morning.

12:35.761 --> 12:37.180
Hey.

12:37.263 --> 12:39.265
Hey, Coach, what's up?

12:39.348 --> 12:43.895
Is there anybody who wants a ticket
to the girls' first Winter Cup game?

12:44.520 --> 12:49.400
My wife bought the ticket,
but her mother hurt her back,

12:49.484 --> 12:51.319
so she had to go home to help.

12:51.402 --> 12:53.571
It's a great courtside seat.

12:53.654 --> 12:55.907
Yes, me, me, me! I want it!

12:57.074 --> 13:00.411
That's fine by me,
but don't you have practice?

13:00.495 --> 13:04.874
Well, it's not for me but for my friend.

13:06.250 --> 13:08.628
I'll take it, then.

13:11.088 --> 13:13.549
I mean, I can actually go.

13:13.633 --> 13:15.051
I don't care either way.

13:15.134 --> 13:16.636
Absolutely not!

13:16.719 --> 13:17.803
Why not?

13:17.887 --> 13:21.390
Feels like it'd be more beneficial to me
since I'm on the basketball team.

13:21.474 --> 13:23.518
I called dibs first!

13:23.601 --> 13:26.062
He never mentioned
first come, first served.

13:26.896 --> 13:31.526
<i>I just don't want him getting close
to Chinatsu Senpai!</i>

13:31.609 --> 13:34.195
Ever heard of the saying,
"The early bird gets the worm"?

13:34.278 --> 13:37.907
It's been a while
since I heard that in Japanese.

13:37.990 --> 13:40.743
<i>There he goes,
bragging about living abroad again!</i>

13:41.494 --> 13:43.746
Anyway, do whatever you want with it.

13:44.330 --> 13:46.624
Okay, how about we compete for it?

13:47.208 --> 13:50.127
Like, maybe

13:50.211 --> 13:54.131
whoever can last longer
doing a shuttle run wins.

13:54.715 --> 13:56.008
Shuttle run?

13:56.092 --> 14:00.805
I figured running would be fairer
than doing each other's sports.

14:00.888 --> 14:02.974
And we just need to run back and forth.

14:04.850 --> 14:09.605
Wait, basketball players
should naturally have more endurance.

14:09.689 --> 14:11.566
Plus, he's older.

14:11.649 --> 14:15.403
And he mentioned running 10 kilometers
every day when he was in America.

14:15.486 --> 14:18.656
Hard to imagine
that this doesn't favor Matsuoka.

14:19.699 --> 14:20.825
What do you say?

14:22.326 --> 14:23.494
I'll do it!

14:25.037 --> 14:30.293
<i>A five-second countdown will be given,
after which the test will begin.</i>

14:31.752 --> 14:32.920
<i>Five seconds to start.</i>

14:33.504 --> 14:36.424
<i>Three, two, one.</i>

14:36.507 --> 14:37.508
<i>Start!</i>

14:52.189 --> 14:54.942
Now we're going back to school
to practice?

14:55.026 --> 14:57.320
I already feel like I gave it my all
at the practice game.

14:57.403 --> 15:00.072
Well, we can work on
our issues right away.

15:00.156 --> 15:03.242
They could at least send a bus for us.

15:03.326 --> 15:05.328
Well, it's within walking distance.

15:08.623 --> 15:12.084
I'm going to swing by my home
to pick up a change of clothes first.

15:12.168 --> 15:13.669
Okay, got it.

15:23.429 --> 15:28.351
KIKUCHI DENTAL CLINIC

15:28.434 --> 15:31.604
<i>This is the dentist
that Taiki is going to.</i>

15:31.687 --> 15:34.357
You definitely shouldn't go!

15:34.440 --> 15:37.026
Thanks for taking care of this.

15:37.109 --> 15:39.570
I'll be back in about 30 minutes.

15:41.322 --> 15:42.907
See you in a few...

15:49.038 --> 15:50.247
Wait, Ms. Goto.

15:50.331 --> 15:53.626
Could you pick up toilet paper as well?

15:53.709 --> 15:54.585
Sure.

15:58.130 --> 15:59.131
Goto?

16:01.842 --> 16:04.136
I thought your last name was Kido.

16:05.221 --> 16:09.392
My parents got divorced
when I graduated from junior high.

16:10.518 --> 16:12.395
I didn't know that.

16:13.104 --> 16:17.191
It's no big deal,
so I didn't think it was worth mentioning.

16:19.068 --> 16:23.114
You really never tell me anything.

16:33.624 --> 16:37.670
Does he want the ticket that bad?

16:37.753 --> 16:39.839
Is it really worth running that much for?

16:40.548 --> 16:43.300
It's obviously something more than that.

16:43.801 --> 16:44.802
What do you mean?

16:45.386 --> 16:47.805
I bet your legs are starting
to feel heavy.

16:47.888 --> 16:49.807
I can do this all day!

16:51.809 --> 16:55.730
Good, because this is barely
even a warm-up for me.

16:56.313 --> 16:58.482
<i>He seems confident.</i>

17:00.568 --> 17:03.320
While we're at it,

17:03.404 --> 17:08.325
how about the loser gives up
on Natsu, too?

17:10.745 --> 17:13.039
There's no way I'd agree to that.

17:14.540 --> 17:17.334
My feelings are too strong to give up
over something this stupid!

17:18.002 --> 17:19.336
I see.

17:20.046 --> 17:21.047
But...

17:24.341 --> 17:30.056
even if you don't agree to it,
you'd look pretty lame losing to me here.

17:37.229 --> 17:39.356
You never tell me anything.

17:46.530 --> 17:48.282
Are you working here?

17:50.493 --> 17:51.410
Yeah.

17:52.703 --> 17:54.997
<i>Then Taiki must have known already.</i>

17:59.001 --> 18:03.172
Are your parents the reason why
you transferred to another high school?

18:03.964 --> 18:05.633
That has nothing to do with it.

18:06.383 --> 18:07.676
I see.

18:08.469 --> 18:12.223
I wish you would've told me these things.

18:13.390 --> 18:15.226
But just because I'm your friend,

18:15.309 --> 18:17.520
it doesn't mean
you have to tell me everything.

18:18.062 --> 18:21.190
And I don't want to act like
I know how you feel.

18:22.233 --> 18:24.193
It's your life after all.

18:24.985 --> 18:26.695
You didn't have a choice, right?

18:34.036 --> 18:36.372
Sorry for interrupting your shopping.

18:39.542 --> 18:40.835
How could I tell you?!

18:44.296 --> 18:45.923
<i>I could never be vulnerable!</i>

18:46.590 --> 18:47.925
<i>Not in front of you!</i>

18:52.263 --> 18:54.932
Because I was your role model!

19:00.020 --> 19:04.942
It goes without saying,
we had some fun times as friends, too.

19:05.025 --> 19:10.531
<i>You looked up to me for being someone
who was good at basketball.</i>

19:11.031 --> 19:12.950
<i>At first, that made me happy.</i>

19:14.034 --> 19:19.206
But then gradually,
my passion for basketball faded.

19:21.584 --> 19:22.877
You're lying.

19:22.960 --> 19:24.545
I'm not lying.

19:28.883 --> 19:31.969
Listen, Yumeka, your father and I...

19:33.137 --> 19:36.473
I'm not as cool as you think I am.

19:37.183 --> 19:39.894
<i>I constantly felt like skipping practice.</i>

19:40.519 --> 19:45.900
<i>Once I realized talent didn't matter,
I wanted to run away from basketball.</i>

19:47.318 --> 19:51.530
So if anything,
I was the one who looked up to you.

19:53.699 --> 19:55.910
You never even thought
about skipping practice.

19:56.535 --> 19:58.913
You were always so focused
on what you needed to work on,

19:58.996 --> 20:00.206
and I couldn't keep up.

20:00.706 --> 20:03.667
I was embarrassed
by how different I was from you,

20:04.251 --> 20:06.295
<i>and I started resenting you.</i>

20:08.088 --> 20:10.174
How could I tell you any of that?

20:13.844 --> 20:16.305
But I do admire

20:16.805 --> 20:18.474
her ability to work hard.

20:19.225 --> 20:22.686
Being able to do that is your talent.

20:25.731 --> 20:28.442
I saw you.

20:29.151 --> 20:31.946
<i>The day after our final game
in junior high school.</i>

20:37.159 --> 20:39.536
<i>I saw you practicing by yourself.</i>

20:41.455 --> 20:44.625
I was in a slump around then

20:44.708 --> 20:48.087
and even felt a sense of release
when it was all over.

20:50.965 --> 20:54.093
You must've been really disappointed.

20:54.176 --> 20:58.347
To think you must've worked so hard
to be that disappointed...

21:02.184 --> 21:04.895
That's why I was so shocked.

21:05.562 --> 21:08.107
<i>Seeing you hanging out with a boy.</i>

21:08.899 --> 21:13.612
<i>That's not the Natsu
I felt so inferior to.</i>

21:13.696 --> 21:17.700
Being crazy about basketball,
unable to think about anything unrelated,

21:17.783 --> 21:19.994
<i>quietly putting in the work.</i>

21:20.077 --> 21:21.745
That's who you are!

21:21.829 --> 21:23.122
You're wrong!

21:25.207 --> 21:26.875
It's not unrelated.

21:28.460 --> 21:31.380
<i>They're one and the same to me.</i>

21:34.717 --> 21:36.385
After you quit,

21:37.094 --> 21:42.391
<i>I lost the goal I had been chasing,
and the person I relied on the most.</i>

21:44.059 --> 21:45.561
I was so lonely.

21:48.939 --> 21:51.900
<i>Winning nationals was a distant goal.</i>

21:52.943 --> 21:58.157
<i>And right when I started to doubt
if this kind of steady practice</i>

21:58.240 --> 21:59.908
<i>was really actually helping...</i>

22:04.997 --> 22:06.915
<i>Right when I was starting to break,</i>

22:09.168 --> 22:10.919
<i>I was given the strength.</i>

22:15.632 --> 22:17.926
<i>Having someone like that in my life</i>

22:18.510 --> 22:20.471
is what gave me the drive to keep going!

23:48.892 --> 23:53.897
Subtitle translation by: Zensho Yamamoto
